# RQ3-STABILITY violation in `hwpe_core_mux_ooo`: winner-takes-all ignores no-grant condition

- Source URL: https://github.com/pulp-platform/hci/issues/34

![image](https://github.com/pulp-platform/hci/assets/7882682/b2e9848c-ce99-46fb-8da0-1a36dc453642)

In some instances, when the `in_req` changes in absence of a `gnt` on the pop side, the MUX will switch priorities incorrectly.

PR Title: Fix #34 by keeping winner_d stable in OOO Mux if there is an input request

PR #37 (Merged May 23, 2024)

Author: FrancescoConti

Description:
The pull request addresses a stability issue by preventing re-evaluation of the winner-takes-all output except under specific conditions. According to the author: "Only re-evaluate WTA output after an output handshake or if any in_req was 0, otherwise a more recent in_req could overtake an older one causing a RQ3-STABILITY issue on the output side."

The author notes this represents a rebase of a previous attempt (PR #36) onto the current master branch.

Comments:

FrancescoConti:
Commented that the change prevents a scenario where newer input requests could improperly supersede older ones, which would violate stability requirements on the output side of the multiplexer.

